CSI Driver means Container Storage Interface Driver.

In simple words:

CSI driver is the component that allows Kubernetes to communicate with the actual storage system.

Example in AWS:

Pod
 ↓
PVC
 ↓
PV
 ↓
CSI Driver
 ↓
AWS EBS Volume

The CSI driver handles things like:

Create a volume
Attach volume to a node
Mount volume into a Pod
Detach/unmount volume

For AWS, a common CSI driver is the EBS CSI Driver.

So remember:

PVC = asks for storage
PV = represents storage
CSI driver = connects Kubernetes to the actual storage
EBS = actual storage



